Here is a fix to a warning emited by the latest sensors-detect script
(using perl 5.6.1).
(Warning: Use of "localtime" without parens is ambiguous at
/usr/local/sbin/sensors-detect line 3036.)

I don't see why it is ambiguous, but adding the parens makes perl more
quiet ;)
-- 
Jean "Khali" Delvare
http://www.ensicaen.ismra.fr/~delvare/
-------------- next part --------------
--- sensors-detect.orig	Mon Jul  1 01:57:34 2002
+++ sensors-detect	Tue Jul  9 23:10:25 2002
@@ -3033,7 +3033,7 @@
 #
 EOT
       print SYSCONFIG
-       "# Generated by sensors-detect on " . scalar localtime . "\n";
+       "# Generated by sensors-detect on " . scalar localtime() . "\n";
       my @modules = grep /^modprobe /, split "\n", $modprobes;
       my $i = 1;
       my $sysconfig = "";
